{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1172067,"ns":0,"title":"Catch-22 (logic)","extract":"A catch-22 is a paradoxical situation from which an individual cannot escape because of contradictory rules or limitations. The term was first used by Joseph Heller in his 1961 novel Catch-22.","description":"Situation in which one cannot avoid a problem because of contradictory constraints","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}